{"kind":"article","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Find the factories that depend on each other in a loop.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-you-see","text":"What you see","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In debug builds, resolving a factory that is already being resolved further up the same chain stops at once and prints the cycle:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["Dependency cycle detected: CycleA depends on itself.","  CycleA  (resolved at AppView.swift:20 in body)","  → CycleB  (resolved at CycleA.swift:12 in CycleA)","  → CycleA  (resolved at CycleB.swift:15 in CycleB)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without the check, a sync cycle overflows the stack and an async "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cached"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".shared"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle hangs. Release builds skip it."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-counts-as-a-cycle","text":"What counts as a cycle","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only resolutions that can never finish are reported: the same factory, in the same container, resolved again while its own resolution is still waiting for the result. That covers direct calls, sync and async, and the task a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cached"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".shared"},{"type":"text","text":" scope awaits for an async resolver."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These are not reported:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A back-reference resolved from a "},{"code":"Task { }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that the owner starts but doesn’t wait on, including the tasks "},{"code":"@ConstructorInjected","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@LazyInjected","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" start for async factories. That resolution can still finish."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cycles through ","type":"text"},{"code":"async let","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", task groups, or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the resolver awaits. Swift can’t tell those tasks apart from ones nobody waits on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An async "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cached"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".shared"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle that two callers enter at the same time from different factories, one resolving A then B while the other resolves B then A. Each scope’s task carries only the chain of the caller that started it, so the two wait on each other and hang."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two types that inject each other with macros also need explicit factory types to compile; see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DependencyInjection\/documentation\/DependencyInjection\/InjectionMacros","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"DependencyInjection"}],"title":"Dependency cycles","roleHeading":"Article"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/dependencyinjection\/dependencycycles"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DependencyInjection\/documentation\/DependencyInjection\/DependencyCycles"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Containers and concurrency","anchor":"Containers-and-concurrency","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DependencyInjection\/documentation\/DependencyInjection\/HierarchicalContainers","doc:\/\/DependencyInjection\/documentation\/DependencyInjection\/ContextPropagation"],"generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/DependencyInjection\/documentation\/DependencyInjection"]]},"references":{"doc://DependencyInjection/documentation/DependencyInjection/InjectionMacros":{"title":"Injection macros","identifier":"doc:\/\/DependencyInjection\/documentation\/DependencyInjection\/InjectionMacros","url":"\/documentation\/dependencyinjection\/injectionmacros","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject dependencies into properties with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Injected"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ConstructorInjected"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LazyInjected"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://DependencyInjection/documentation/DependencyInjection/ContextPropagation":{"abstract":[{"text":"Carry the current container into work that structured concurrency doesn’t reach.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/dependencyinjection\/contextpropagation","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Detached tasks and context propagation","identifier":"doc:\/\/DependencyInjection\/documentation\/DependencyInjection\/ContextPropagation"},"doc://DependencyInjection/documentation/DependencyInjection":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Dependency injection for Swift 6, with async factories, injection macros and test containers that stay isolated when tests run in parallel."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DependencyInjection\/documentation\/DependencyInjection","url":"\/documentation\/dependencyinjection","title":"DependencyInjection","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://DependencyInjection/documentation/DependencyInjection/HierarchicalContainers":{"url":"\/documentation\/dependencyinjection\/hierarchicalcontainers","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Hierarchical containers","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Override registrations in a nested scope without touching the enclosing one.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DependencyIn